<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dirk I, Count of Holland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 922</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dirk I (died c. 939) is regarded as the first Count of Holland. In 922 the West Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple">Charles the Simple</a> granted him land around the church of Egmond, the earliest record of the dynasty's power in the region then called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-frisia">West Frisia</a>. His descendants ruled as counts of Holland until the male line died out in 1299.</p></div>
